<title>SINGAPORE: Huan Hsin gets nod for Singapore listing.</title>
<headline>Huan Hsin gets nod for Singapore listing.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Huan Hsin Holdings, which makes wires and cables for the telecommunications industry, said on Thursday it has won approval in principle for a U.S. dollar listing on the main board of the Stock Exchange of Singapore.</p>
<p>The group made pre-tax profit of US$7.2 million in 1996 on the back of a turnover of US$33.8 million.</p>
<p>Huan Hsin has plants in China and Malaysia and its plans include expanding manufacturing facilities in Shanghai.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
